A respected engineer and mother of two young children, has been offered a three-year position leading a sustainable infrastructure project in another country. Her employer will provide relocation support, schooling, and family housing. Her partner is willing to move and manage childcare. Community elders and some local officials express concern, saying mothers of young children should remain at home to uphold family stability, while others praise her as a role model for professional equality.

            If you were advising local authorities on whether public institutions should support such decisions, what would you recommend?:
            "A" = Fully support her choice—women should be free to pursue professional opportunities regardless of parental status.
"B" = Discourage support—mothers of young children have a duty to prioritize family stability over career ambitions abroad.
"C" = Provide neutral information but avoid endorsing or facilitating the move.
"D" = Offer limited support only if she leaves the children in the care of relatives at home.
"E" = Support the decision as long as family needs are carefully considered.

